{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422346-recreating-the-hammersmith-or-galatea-event","id":1422346,"title":"recreating the Hammersmith or Galatea event","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-06T17:45:27-08:00","id":1422346,"title":"recreating the Hammersmith or Galatea event","content":"So, a few thoughts and questoins. If a nova crafter wanted to recreate the Hammersmith event, how hard would it be?<br /> <br /> The event itself happened Pre-nova's, so it should be something within the reach of baselines (albeit it was an accident), and post Galatea, there are no Doyen barriers to worry about. So could a megaintelligent crafter come up with something like that?<br /> <br /> Related to that, what about some form of process to initiate an eruption i a latent nova or even a baseline? Given the core books list, my assumption is that something to cause a <i>random</i> eruption in an individual, would be probably rank 7-8, while something that allowed you to infuse someone who normally couldn't erupt or <i>control</i> the eruption of a nova, would be a nine, and probably a nine with boatload of additions to it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T17:53:49-08:00","id":1422348,"title":"","content":"Without the Barrier you wouldn't need some of the Galatea events level to have the same effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T19:15:10-08:00","id":1422359,"title":"","content":"Also remember the Hammersmith event triggered all three types but mostly Talents and Galatea triggered novas. There was a third event in 2104 set off by Dr. Sara Bhurano that triggered psiads and basically started the Aeon era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T19:32:08-08:00","id":1422362,"title":"","content":"The Galatea era event didn't actually disrupt the Doyen barrier. If that had happened, the Doyen would have noticed and immediately played a game of Rocks Fall, Everyone Dies with humanity. It wasn't until Dr. Bhurano's noetic beacon event that the Earth attracted their attention again. This can be seen on page 368 of the Aeon book: &quot;When she set off the noetic beacon that cleansed the Corrupted zones and attracted the Doyen...&quot;. At that point, the Doyen couldn't immediately eliminate Earth, since roughly two thousand Novas/Aberrants had already fled the planet; they needed Earth's psychics to fight the Aberrants for them.<br /> <br /> And in this specific instance, they may have been right to consider quantum beings as a direct threat to their species, based on page 273 of the Aberrant pdf. If the comic pages are to be believed, Divis Mal was fully aware that aliens were impeding humanity's quantum empowerment. While he mentally bragged about shattering their cocoon, he may have purposefully limited his empowerment event's scope to keep from alerting them that their gambit had failed and humans were erupting in large numbers. Maybe Divis Mal didn't just disappear to hit Quantum 10 and ascend, maybe he's stalking the Doyen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T19:34:23-08:00","id":1422363,"title":"","content":"Bhurano event in 2104 triggered Psiads and Talents and reduced the total Quantum level (reducing the QFZ by a big deal).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T19:40:15-08:00","id":1422365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422346-recreating-the-hammersmith-or-galatea-event?p=1422362#post1422362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Galatea era event didn't actually disrupt the Doyen barrier. If that had happened, the Doyen would have noticed and immediately played a game of Rocks Fall, Everyone Dies with humanity. It wasn't until Dr. Bhurano's noetic beacon event that the Earth attracted their attention again. This can be seen on page 368 of the Aeon book: &quot;When she set off the noetic beacon that cleansed the Corrupted zones and attracted the Doyen...&quot;. At that point, the Doyen couldn't immediately eliminate Earth, since roughly two thousand Novas/Aberrants had already fled the planet; they needed Earth's psychics to fight the Aberrants for them.<br /> <br /> And in this specific instance, they may have been right to consider quantum beings as a direct threat to their species, based on page 273 of the Aberrant pdf. If the comic pages are to be believed, Divis Mal was fully aware that aliens were impeding humanity's quantum empowerment. While he mentally bragged about shattering their cocoon, he may have purposefully limited his empowerment event's scope to keep from alerting them that their gambit had failed and humans were erupting in large numbers. Maybe Divis Mal didn't just disappear to hit Quantum 10 and ascend, maybe he's stalking the Doyen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Divis Mal did break the barrier, but as the quantum was so high and so concentrated on Earth it was absolutely impossible for them to stay there or even think about reacting to the Novas. When Bhurano cleansed with her experiment, it turned the game in their favor and allow them to come and create a weapon to fight the Novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T20:11:39-08:00","id":1422367,"title":"","content":"Even if they couldn't actually approach Earth, that would have done nothing to stop them from dropping multiple extinction level asteroids on the planet. Or - later on - doing the same thing to all the colony worlds that would have lacked such concentrated quantum levels.<br /> <br /> And the book does specifically state that Dr. Bhurano &quot;attracted the Doyen&quot;. There would have been no need for that if they were already paying attention due to Divis Mal's quantum empowerment event. The fact that the Doyen didn't show up until after the noetic beacon went off combined with the fact that the Doyen did nothing about the 2000+ Aberrants who'd left Earth 37 years earlier indicates rather strongly that they didn't know what was happening. The galaxy is a big, big place, and they were presumably busy doing other things while assuming the dampening cocoon they placed around Earth was doing its job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-06T23:50:05-08:00","id":1422389,"title":"","content":"Also bear in mind (I think) that the destruction of the Galatea was really just a side effect of the Quantum wave caused by Divis Mal\u2019s experiment, not its ultimate cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T00:03:19-08:00","id":1422391,"title":"","content":"The Galatea blew up as a result of a Nova erupting on it, iirc? Who then wound up floating around in orbit, alive, sustained by their powers but without having gained the ability to fly or effectively signal their location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T03:43:46-08:00","id":1422407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422346-recreating-the-hammersmith-or-galatea-event?p=1422391#post1422391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Galatea blew up as a result of a Nova erupting on it, iirc? Who then wound up floating around in orbit, alive, sustained by their powers but without having gained the ability to fly or effectively signal their location.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. But it wasn\u2019t the cause of the Quantum wave that engulfed Earth like people thought. Divis Mal was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T03:44:47-08:00","id":1422408,"title":"","content":"Although wouldn\u2019t satellite cameras eventually see this guy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-07T22:57:30-08:00","id":1422553,"title":"","content":"Maybe, but it might take them a while- space is big. They'd probably be tracking the debris from the Galatea explosion just because of the risk of Kessler syndrome, but public attention's going to be distracted by the start of Nova eruptions on Earth. Then they'd have to figure out that &quot;person-sized chunk of debris&quot; is in fact a person, at which point the natural assumption is that it's just a body. <br /> <br /> Ironically, I can see people debating whether to retrieve the supposed corpse for burial or let it remain &quot;buried&quot; in space undisturbed as an honor. <br /> <br /> Finding out that the former astronaut is actually alive might take quite some time indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-08T14:24:04-08:00","id":1422662,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I totally forgot about him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-09T01:15:32-08:00","id":1422707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422346-recreating-the-hammersmith-or-galatea-event?p=1422362#post1422362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Galatea era event didn't actually disrupt the Doyen barrier. If that had happened, the Doyen would have noticed and immediately played a game of Rocks Fall, Everyone Dies with humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book does explicitly say that Divis Mal broke the Doyen barrier with the events of N-Day. Check the Secrets section on page 275 where it says that &quot;he and his allies managed to recreate their own version of the Hammersmith experiment, unleashing a quantum wave that shattered the Doyen energy barrier around the Earth and triggered the nova potential latent in a portion of humanity.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T14:38:27-08:00","id":1423373,"title":"","content":"I thought the barrier around the solar system was Quantum in nature and set up by the more benevolent evacuating Novas after the Ultimatum? That's why a Noetic pulse to heal the earth's corruption zones disrupted it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T05:41:48-08:00","id":1423532,"title":"","content":"There were, as I understand it, two seperate barriers. The first one was a Noetic barrier placed by the Doyen that Divis Mal broke with the Galatea explosion of quantum energy, and then a quantum barrier erected by Novas that was destroyed by SK's Noetic explosion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T08:14:15-08:00","id":1423558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422346-recreating-the-hammersmith-or-galatea-event?p=1423532#post1423532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were, as I understand it, two seperate barriers. The first one was a Noetic barrier placed by the Doyen that Divis Mal broke with the Galatea explosion of quantum energy, and then a quantum barrier erected by Novas that was destroyed by SK's Noetic explosion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What's the narrative role the first and its fall plays? Nothing came in from outside in response to its fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T08:27:24-08:00","id":1423562,"title":"","content":"The Doyen's barrier was there to suppress the expression of human potential towards Quantum. It is the reason we did not see many novas until Mal broke the barrier by attempting to recreate the Hammersmith experiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T10:11:19-08:00","id":1423584,"title":"","content":"Mal knew about the Doyen barrier, and probably the reason for the results were so powerful was exactly the fact he needed to breach the barrier to be able to affect the entire world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T11:30:18-08:00","id":1423606,"title":"","content":"Divis Mal knowing about the doyen barrier makes me wish that instead of him simply leaving at the end of the Aberrant War he instead literally used his quantum god-power to basically stop them or destroy them or protect the Earth in a way that means they couldn't do what they did. <br /> <br /> By the way, I really hate the Doyen, they are like the Ori from Stargate and need to be destroyed like the Ori are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T12:12:59-08:00","id":1423614,"title":"","content":"Seems like the last thing he'd do. Humans want a destiny apart from Novas? Fine- they can solve their own problems with the Doyen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T12:14:07-08:00","id":1423615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422346-recreating-the-hammersmith-or-galatea-event?p=1423606#post1423606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Divis Mal knowing about the doyen barrier makes me wish that instead of him simply leaving at the end of the Aberrant War he instead literally used his quantum god-power to basically stop them or destroy them or protect the Earth in a way that means they couldn't do what they did.<br /> <br /> By the way, I really hate the Doyen, they are like the Ori from Stargate and need to be destroyed like the Ori are.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it makes you feel better, tonight I'm running a session of Aeon where the Doyen are going to use a Chromatic fleet to attack Eden with the players caught in the middle. It should culminate in a giant rift in time and space which will put the game on hold and allow us to play some other TC games, all of which will culminate in a giant rift in time and space. Then we'll have a Crisis on Infinite Trinity Continuum Games game to resolve all of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T12:33:26-08:00","id":1423620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422346-recreating-the-hammersmith-or-galatea-event?p=1423615#post1423615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it makes you feel better, tonight I'm running a session of Aeon where the Doyen are going to use a Chromatic fleet to attack Eden with the players caught in the middle. It should culminate in a giant rift in time and space which will put the game on hold and allow us to play some other TC games, all of which will culminate in a giant rift in time and space. Then we'll have a Crisis on Infinite Trinity Continuum Games game to resolve all of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is... just... AWESOME!<br /> Inam working now on a Core campaign that soon will turn into a Aberrant campaign. Not that the plates characters will erupt, as they are talents, but they will reach 2018 and follow novas erupting and later we will change the characters for novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T13:37:22-08:00","id":1423627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1422346-recreating-the-hammersmith-or-galatea-event?p=1423562#post1423562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Doyen's barrier was there to suppress the expression of human potential towards Quantum. It is the reason we did not see many novas until Mal broke the barrier by attempting to recreate the Hammersmith experiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not just quantum. The Doyen barrier muffled any 'flux' event, limiting the propagation of Nova, Psiad, and Talent powers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}